  "name": "Parental support: how much the sibling split matters",
  "description": "The same household and the same two tail trajectories, against every plausible split with Simone's sister. Housing is held at the Cherry Hill $655k house so the split is the only thing moving. The point of the grid is the asymmetry: halving the share of a US nursing-care trajectory is worth far more than the entire difference between the three houses, while halving the share of a Brazilian one is worth almost nothing. Where the parents age determines whether the sibling negotiation is a financial conversation at all.",
